---
title: Two-Tier Extraction Data Flow
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User taps article
    participant APS as ArticlePipelineService
    participant CE as CloudExtractionService
    participant Proxy as extract-proxy Lambda
    participant DDB as DynamoDB<br/>extraction-index
    participant S3 as S3 Bucket
    participant LightQ as SQS Light Queue
    participant Light as extract-light<br/>(jsdom + Readability)
    participant PuppetQ as SQS Puppeteer Queue
    participant Fargate as ECS Fargate<br/>(Puppeteer + Chrome)
    participant Web as Article Website
    participant NSC as NSCache (L1)
    participant SD as SwiftData (L2)
    participant WK as WKWebView (L3)

    User->>APS: process(item)

    Note over APS: Check L1 memory cache first
    APS->>NSC: lookup by item ID
    NSC-->>APS: miss

    Note over APS: Premium user: check L0 cloud cache
    APS->>CE: fetch(articleURL, itemID, feedName)
    CE->>Proxy: GET /v1/extract/{sha256(url)}
    Proxy->>DDB: GetItem(urlHash)

    alt L0 Cache Hit
        DDB-->>Proxy: s3Key found
        Proxy->>S3: GetObject
        S3-->>Proxy: ContentNode JSON
        Proxy-->>CE: 200 + ExtractedArticle
        CE-->>APS: article (title, author, hero, nodes)
        Note over APS: ~80ms total
        APS->>NSC: store in L1
        APS->>SD: store in L2
        APS-->>User: display article

    else L0 Cache Miss (202 Queued)
        DDB-->>Proxy: not found
        Proxy->>LightQ: enqueue {urlHash, url}
        Proxy-->>CE: 202 {status: "queued", retryAfterSeconds: 5}

        Note over CE: Wait 5 seconds, retry once
        CE->>CE: sleep(5s)
        CE->>Proxy: GET /v1/extract/{hash} (retry)

        alt Retry Hit (extraction completed)
            Proxy->>DDB: GetItem
            DDB-->>Proxy: s3Key found
            Proxy->>S3: GetObject
            Proxy-->>CE: 200 + ExtractedArticle
            CE-->>APS: article
            APS-->>User: display article
        else Retry Miss
            Proxy-->>CE: 202 still queued
            CE-->>APS: nil (fall through)
        end

        Note over APS: Fall through to local extraction
        APS->>SD: check L2 (SwiftData disk cache)
        SD-->>APS: miss
        APS->>WK: L3: WKWebView + Readability.js
        WK->>Web: load page + render JS
        Web-->>WK: HTML
        WK-->>APS: ContentNode[]
        Note over APS: 3-8 seconds
        APS->>NSC: store in L1
        APS->>SD: store in L2
        APS-->>User: display article
    end

    par Server-side extraction (async, in background)
        LightQ->>Light: dequeue {urlHash, url}
        Light->>Web: fetch HTML (10s timeout)
        Light->>Light: jsdom + Readability.parse()
        Light->>Light: inferTopics(title, content)
        Light->>Light: extractHeroImage(og:image)

        alt Content >= 100 words
            Light->>Light: htmlToContentNodes()
            Light->>S3: PutObject articles/{hash}.json
            Light->>DDB: PutItem urlHash → s3Key (72h TTL)
            Light->>DDB: UPDATE feed_items (word_count, topics)
            Note over Light: jsdom path: ~200ms, $0.0000004
        else Content < 100 words (SPA site)
            Note over Light: Thin content — needs JS rendering
            Light->>PuppetQ: enqueue to Puppeteer
            PuppetQ->>Fargate: dequeue
            Fargate->>Web: Puppeteer loads page (2s JS wait)
            Fargate->>Fargate: Readability.parse()
            Fargate->>S3: store ContentNode JSON
            Fargate->>DDB: index urlHash
            Note over Fargate: Puppeteer path: ~5-10s, ~$0.03
        end
    end
